  "title": "Kirby Problem 2.34",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $S$ be a compact surface. For $0 \\leq r < s$, does there exist a\nnontrivial finitely generated subgroup $G_{r} \\leq \\operatorname{Diff}^{r}_{0}(S)$ such that every action of $G_{r}$\non $S$ by $C^{s}$ diffeomorphisms is trivial? Can these examples be torsion-free?",
